Input: {"question": "What position does Emmanuel de Sainte-Hermine currently or formerly hold?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 26, "text": "Emmanuel de Sainte-Hermine"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 28, "end": 203, "text": "Emmanuel de Sainte-Hermine (1770-1850) was a French politician who held the unique position of desservant, a Catholic priest in charge of a parish but not officially a parson."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 204, "end": 225, "text": "Early Life and Career"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 227, "end": 342, "text": "Born in 1770, Sainte-Hermine was raised in a devout Catholic family and showed an early interest in the priesthood."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 343, "end": 427, "text": "He studied theology at the University of Paris and was ordained as a priest in 1795."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 428, "end": 446, "text": "Rise to Prominence"}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 448, "end": 590, "text": "Sainte-Hermine's rise to prominence began during the French Revolution, when he became a vocal advocate for the rights of the Catholic Church."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 591, "end": 728, "text": "His eloquence and charisma earned him the attention of Napoleon Bonaparte, who appointed him as a member of the Council of State in 1804."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 729, "end": 751, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 753, "end": 826, "text": "Several studies have confirmed Sainte-Hermine's position as a desservant."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 827, "end": 1068, "text": "A 2007 study published in the Journal of French Ecclesiastical History found that Sainte-Hermine was responsible for the spiritual well-being of the parish of Saint-Germain-des-Prés in Paris, despite not holding the official title of parson."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1069, "end": 1072, "text": "[1]"}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1074, "end": 1302, "text": "A biography of Sainte-Hermine published in 2012 by French historian Pierre Dupont further supports this claim, citing archival records that demonstrate Sainte-Hermine's role in administering the parish and performing sacraments."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1303, "end": 1306, "text": "[2]"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1308, "end": 1576, "text": "A 2015 article in the Catholic Historical Review also notes Sainte-Hermine's unique position, stating that \"while not officially recognized as a parson, Sainte-Hermine's duties and responsibilities were identical to those of a parson, making him a de facto desservant."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1577, "end": 1581, "text": "\"[3]"}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1583, "end": 1589, "text": "Legacy"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1591, "end": 1689, "text": "Sainte-Hermine's legacy as a desservant has had a lasting impact on the Catholic Church in France."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1690, "end": 1788, "text": "His commitment to the faith and his community has inspired generations of priests and politicians."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1789, "end": 1799, "text": "References"}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1801, "end": 1934, "text": "[1] \"The Ecclesiastical Career of Emmanuel de Sainte-Hermine\" by Marie-Thérèse Ravier, Journal of French Ecclesiastical History, Vol."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1935, "end": 1942, "text": "28, No."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 26, "text": "Emmanuel de Sainte-Hermine"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 28, "end": 177, "text": "Emmanuel de Sainte-Hermine (1770-1850) was a French politician who held the position of member of the Chamber of Peers during the early 19th century."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 178, "end": 199, "text": "Early Life and Career"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 201, "end": 311, "text": "Born in 1770, Sainte-Hermine came from a noble family and was educated in the traditional aristocratic manner."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 312, "end": 427, "text": "He began his political career during the French Revolution, serving as a deputy to the National Convention in 1792."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 428, "end": 572, "text": "[1] After the fall of the monarchy, Sainte-Hermine aligned himself with the moderate Girondin faction, advocating for a constitutional monarchy."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 573, "end": 576, "text": "[2]"}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 578, "end": 596, "text": "Rise to Prominence"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 598, "end": 729, "text": "Following Napoleon Bonaparte's coup d'état in 1799, Sainte-Hermine adapted to the new regime and became a supporter of the Emperor."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 730, "end": 857, "text": "He was appointed to the Council of State in 1804 and later served as Prefect of the Seine-et-Oise department from 1806 to 1813."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 858, "end": 979, "text": "[3] During this period, Sainte-Hermine demonstrated his administrative skills, earning recognition from Napoleon himself."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 980, "end": 983, "text": "[4]"}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 985, "end": 1015, "text": "Member of the Chamber of Peers"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1017, "end": 1127, "text": "After Napoleon's abdication in 1814, Sainte-Hermine was appointed to the Chamber of Peers by King Louis XVIII."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1128, "end": 1238, "text": "The Chamber of Peers was the upper house of the French parliament, composed of nobles and high-ranking clergy."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1239, "end": 1366, "text": "As a member of the Chamber, Sainte-Hermine played a significant role in shaping French politics during the Bourbon Restoration."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1367, "end": 1370, "text": "[5]"}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1372, "end": 1503, "text": "Throughout his tenure, Sainte-Hermine was known for his moderate stance, often mediating between liberal and conservative factions."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1504, "end": 1642, "text": "He supported the Charter of 1814, which established the constitutional monarchy, and advocated for the protection of individual liberties."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1643, "end": 1646, "text": "[6]"}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1648, "end": 1654, "text": "Legacy"}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1656, "end": 1850, "text": "Emmanuel de Sainte-Hermine's political career spanned over three decades, during which he navigated the complexities of the French Revolution, the Napoleonic Empire, and the Bourbon Restoration."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1851, "end": 1970, "text": "His appointment to the Chamber of Peers cemented his position as a respected and influential figure in French politics."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1971, "end": 1982, "text": "References:"}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1984, "end": 2017, "text": "[1] \"Emmanuel de Sainte-Hermine.\""}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2018, "end": 2038, "text": "Assemblée Nationale."}, "D2S27": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2039, "end": 2060, "text": "Retrieved 2023-02-20."}, "D2S28": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2061, "end": 2077, "text": "[2] \"Girondins.\""}, "D2S29": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2078, "end": 2102, "text": "Encyclopedia Britannica."}, "D2S30": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2103, "end": 2124, "text": "Retrieved 2023-02-20."}, "D2S31": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2125, "end": 2158, "text": "[3] \"Emmanuel de Sainte-Hermine.\""}, "D2S32": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2159, "end": 2179, "text": "Archives Nationales."}}, "candidates": [], "original_cards": [], "initial_answers": ["desservant", "member of the Chamber of Peers", "deputy to the National Convention", "Prefect of the Seine-et-Oise", "member of the Council of State"]}
